      "date": "2026-10-30 07:42:41.000000000",
      "message": "Patch Set 2:\n\n(5 comments)\n\nAI code review results below, please doublecheck\n\nLooks good overall; a few minor points inline for whenever the patch is next refreshed, no need to re-spin for them. Nothing in this patch or in the strict-SOM test added by the next change (sanity-flr test_44h) actually runs \"lfs mirror resync\" or \"lfs mirror verify\" on a file with a SOM mirror, so the RESYNC_DONE and llapi_mirror_resync_many_params() changes here are untested. Could test_44h write to a strict-SOM file and then run \"lfs mirror resync\" twice and \"lfs mirror verify\"?",
      "accounts_in_message": [],
      "_revision_number": 2
    },
